{"_schema":{"name":"good_subsets_registry","version":1,"created":"2026-09-04","study":"benchmarks/subset_quality_study_2026-09-04.md","append_only":true,"what":"One row per (arm, seed) training cell: the DRAWN TRAINING SUBSET that seed produced, fingerprinted, beside the held-out scores the resulting bake achieved. Subsets are reconstructed by replaying the trainer sampler through mlp_train::sampling (the owner), never re-implemented; the replay is proved faithful against a real run via ZENSIM_SAMPLE_DIGEST=1.","finding":"THE STUDY FALSIFIED ITS OWN HYPOTHESIS. Subset coverage does NOT explain seed-to-seed score spread: at production settings (120 x 50k draws over ~700k rows) coverage is SATURATED, and a pure-RNG-luck control descriptor correlates with held-out score at least as strongly as any real coverage descriptor. Do NOT use this registry to pick a seed by its coverage numbers. It is a provenance record and an audit trail, not an oracle.","cell_columns":["arm","bake","sample_seed","init_seed","sample_sequence_digest","cid22_ref","cid22","konjnd","aic3"],"descriptors_not_stored":"The 29 coverage descriptors are NOT duplicated here: they are a deterministic function of the subset, so `subset_sim --fulleval <bake>.fulleval.json --seeds <sample_seed>` regenerates them exactly, and the digest column proves you regenerated the right subset. The computed tables are at _full_table.","seeds_were_fused":"EVERY cell below predates --init-seed/--sample-seed, so its single --seed drove BOTH the init stream and the sample stream; sample_seed and init_seed are equal by construction and the two effects cannot be separated for these rows. Rows added after 2026-09-04 may differ.","key":"sample_seed + sample_sequence_digest identify the subset. init_seed is recorded separately.","fields":{"sample_sequence_digest":"FNV-1a over the (train_pos, ia, ib) draw stream, skips tagged","s":"held-out scores: cid22_ref = within-image CID22 (per_ref_mean); cid22/konjnd/aic3 are signed SROCC. KADID and TID are excluded \u2014 train==val on these arms."},"replay":"subset_sim --fulleval <bake>.fulleval.json --seeds <sample_seed> reproduces any row here; the digest must match.","_full_table":"/mnt/v/output/zensim/subset-study-2026-09-04/ (phase2_rows.json, cov/arm_*.json, phase2_corr.json, phase2_null.json) \u2014 see benchmarks/subset_study_data_2026-09-04.pointer.md"},"arms":[{"arm":0,"k":12,"group_key":"a8d11e93084a","argv_key":"e76fa023e0f3cd0d","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.954417},{"arm":1,"k":12,"group_key":"37c92ec7c6ab","argv_key":"82658ef447cc7782","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.957816},{"arm":3,"k":7,"group_key":"86aea3f56ba9","argv_key":"e714d9340f58e74c","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.957538},{"arm":4,"k":6,"group_key":"6baf14e2f264","argv_key":"98a14d465cdbec54","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.954294},{"arm":5,"k":7,"group_key":"a49acad4d5ab","argv_key":"1173bb3a91b162d3","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.956329},{"arm":8,"k":4,"group_key":"3ad1d8e4a3f3","argv_key":"eb8e92cfa69a022e","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.95936},{"arm":9,"k":3,"group_key":"1f26e83b5539","argv_key":"b510966ec67ed3f1","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.95436},{"arm":11,"k":3,"group_key":"0eb4e33cf9c8","argv_key":"d393d9d92252fff2","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.953596},{"arm":12,"k":3,"group_key":"6fb7fb6c93c4","argv_key":"0012e73fabc137f1","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.957049},{"arm":13,"k":3,"group_key":"55dc699a767a","argv_key":"291a5fe19a9131cd","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.960092},{"arm":14,"k":3,"group_key":"9bbda2ede8b1","argv_key":"8e18f3002651f0ec","n_inputs":944,"epochs":120,"ppe":50000,"cid22_ref_q3":0.956536},{"arm":15,"k":3,"group_key":"3ad1d8e4a3f3","argv_key":"456d0a13ac28e0c4","n_inputs":944,"epochs":1